++@@ -0,0 +1,206 @@
+++# Spec: Configurable Integration URL Defaults (EPMCDME-10928)
+++
+++## Problem
+++
+++~20 integration `CodeMieToolConfig` subclasses have hardcoded URL placeholders and/or pre-filled default values. These cannot be customised per deployment (EPAM, SCOR, etc.) without code changes. Operators have no hook to point integrations at their company's Jira, GitLab, etc. without touching source.
+++
+++## Scope
+++
+++Backend only. No DB migrations, no API contract changes, no UI changes this session.
+++
+++---
+++
+++## Design
+++
+++### Core mechanism
+++
+++One utility function in `src/codemie_tools/base/models.py` (adjacent to `RequiredField`):
+++
+++```python
+++def config_url(config_attr: str) -> str:
+++    from codemie.configs import config as _app_config
+++    return getattr(_app_config, config_attr, "")
+++```
+++
+++Called at **class-definition time** so the value is baked into `Field(...)` metadata before `get_available_tools_configs_info()` populates its LRU cache at startup.
+++
+++The lazy import (`from codemie.configs import config`) avoids circular imports. The `codemie_tools → codemie` dependency has established precedent in `datasources_config.py`.
+++
+++`config.py` is the single source of truth for all default URL values. There is no second "hardcoded fallback" string at each call site — the `Config` field default IS the fallback. If an operator leaves a `DEFAULT_*_TOOL_URL` env var unset, pydantic-settings applies the `config.py` default. If they set it to `""`, they get an empty placeholder — explicit operator intent is respected.
+++
+++### New fields in `Config(BaseSettings)` (`src/codemie/configs/config.py`)
+++
+++All fields default to the conventional/example value; the env var name matches the field name. The `_TOOL_URL` suffix distinguishes these from infrastructure env vars (`ELASTIC_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_URL`, `KUBERNETES_API_URL`, etc.):
+++
+++```python
+++DEFAULT_JIRA_TOOL_URL: str = "https://jira.example.com/"
+++DEFAULT_CONFLUENCE_TOOL_URL: str = "https://confluence.example.com/"
+++DEFAULT_GITLAB_TOOL_URL: str = "https://gitlab.example.com"
+++DEFAULT_GITHUB_TOOL_URL: str = "https://api.github.com"
+++DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL: str = "https://dev.azure.com"
+++DEFAULT_KEYCLOAK_TOOL_URL: str = "https://keycloak.example.com"
+++DEFAULT_ELASTIC_TOOL_URL: str = "https://your-elastic-instance.com"
+++DEFAULT_EMAIL_SMTP_TOOL_URL: str = "smtp.gmail.com:587"
+++DEFAULT_EMAIL_OAUTH_AUTHORITY_TOOL_URL: str = "https://login.microsoftonline.com"
+++DEFAULT_EMAIL_OAUTH_SCOPE_TOOL_URL: str = "https://outlook.office365.com/.default"
+++DEFAULT_XRAY_TOOL_URL: str = "https://xray.cloud.getxray.app"
+++DEFAULT_ZEPHYR_TOOL_URL: str = "https://api.zephyrscale.smartbear.com/v2"
+++DEFAULT_SERVICENOW_TOOL_URL: str = "https://your-instance.service-now.com"
+++DEFAULT_REPORTPORTAL_TOOL_URL: str = "https://reportportal.example.com"
+++DEFAULT_KUBERNETES_TOOL_URL: str = "https://kubernetes.default.svc"
+++DEFAULT_SONAR_TOOL_URL: str = "https://sonarqube.example.com"
+++DEFAULT_XWIKI_TOOL_URL: str = "https://wiki.example.com"
+++DEFAULT_SHAREPOINT_TOOL_URL: str = "https://yourtenant.sharepoint.com"
+++```
+++
+++`DEFAULT_ELASTIC_TOOL_URL` is intentionally distinct from the existing `ELASTIC_URL` (the infrastructure Elasticsearch). The existing `_handle_missing_config` Elastic service-layer fallback remains unchanged.
+++
+++### Two field semantics
+++
+++**A — placeholder-only fields** (`RequiredField`, `default=""`): env var overrides only `placeholder`.
+++
+++```python
+++# Before
+++base_url: str = RequiredField(
+++    description="Xray Cloud base URL",
+++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": "https://xray.cloud.getxray.app"},
+++)
+++
+++# After
+++base_url: str = RequiredField(
+++    description="Xray Cloud base URL",
+++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_XRAY_TOOL_URL")},
+++)
+++```
+++
+++**B — pre-filled default fields** (`Field(default=...)`, real runtime default): env var overrides BOTH `default` and `placeholder` via the same call.
+++
+++```python
+++# Before
+++url: Optional[str] = Field(
+++    default="https://api.github.com",
+++    description="GitHub API URL",
+++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": "https://api.github.com"},
+++)
+++
+++# After
+++url: Optional[str] = Field(
+++    default=config_url("DEFAULT_GITHUB_TOOL_URL"),
+++    description="GitHub API URL",
+++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_GITHUB_TOOL_URL")},
+++)
+++```
+++
+++`EmailToolConfig.oauth_authority` and `EmailToolConfig.oauth_scope` follow the same type B pattern (used at runtime as OAuth flow defaults, relevant for national cloud deployments).
+++
+++---
+++
+++## Integration inventory
+++
+++| Config class | File | URL field | Env var | Semantic |
+++|---|---|---|---|---|
+++| `JiraConfig` | `core/project_management/jira/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_JIRA_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `ConfluenceConfig` | `core/project_management/confluence/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_CONFLUENCE_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `XWikiConfig` | `core/project_management/xwiki/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_XWIKI_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `GitlabConfig` | `core/vcs/gitlab/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_GITLAB_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `GithubConfig` | `core/vcs/github/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_GITHUB_TOOL_URL` | B |
+++| `AzureDevOpsGitConfig` | `core/vcs/azure_devops_git/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `AzureDevOpsWorkItemConfig` | `azure_devops/work_item/models.py` | `organization_url` | `DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `AzureDevOpsWikiConfig` | `azure_devops/wiki/models.py` | `organization_url` | `DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `AzureDevOpsTestPlanConfig` | `azure_devops/test_plan/models.py` | `organization_url` | `DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `KeycloakConfig` | `access_management/keycloak/models.py` | `base_url` | `DEFAULT_KEYCLOAK_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `ElasticConfig` | `data_management/elastic/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_ELASTIC_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `EmailToolConfig` | `notification/email/models.py` | `url` (SMTP) | `DEFAULT_EMAIL_SMTP_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `EmailToolConfig` | same | `oauth_authority` | `DEFAULT_EMAIL_OAUTH_AUTHORITY_TOOL_URL` | B |
+++| `EmailToolConfig` | same | `oauth_scope` | `DEFAULT_EMAIL_OAUTH_SCOPE_TOOL_URL` | B |
+++| `XrayConfig` | `qa/xray/models.py` | `base_url` | `DEFAULT_XRAY_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `ZephyrConfig` | `qa/zephyr/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_ZEPHYR_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `ServiceNowConfig` | `itsm/servicenow/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_SERVICENOW_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `ReportPortalConfig` | `report_portal/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_REPORTPORTAL_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `KubernetesConfig` | `cloud/kubernetes/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_KUBERNETES_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `SonarConfig` | `code/models.py` | `url` | `DEFAULT_SONAR_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++| `SharePointConfig` *(new)* | `data_management/sharepoint/models.py` *(new)* | `url` | `DEFAULT_SHAREPOINT_TOOL_URL` | A |
+++
+++Three Azure DevOps configs share `DEFAULT_AZURE_DEVOPS_TOOL_URL`; operators set one variable for all three.
+++
+++---
+++
+++## Prerequisite changes
+++
+++### ZephyrConfig — add Field metadata without changing required semantics
+++
+++`src/codemie_tools/qa/zephyr/models.py` currently has `url: str` (bare annotation, no `Field`). Pydantic v2 treats this as required — `ZephyrConfig` without `url` raises `ValidationError`. Using `RequiredField` (which sets `default=""`) would silently weaken that to app-level enforcement. Instead, add `Field(...)` with no `default` to preserve the pydantic-required behaviour while adding the placeholder metadata:
+++
+++```python
+++# Before
+++url: str
+++
+++# After — no semantic change, adds placeholder only
+++url: str = Field(
+++    description="Zephyr Scale API URL",
+++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_ZEPHYR_TOOL_URL")},
+++)
+++```
+++
+++### SharePointConfig — new model
+++
+++`SharePointCredentials` (`src/codemie/rest_api/models/settings.py`) is a plain `BaseModel` outside the toolkit hierarchy, so it is not surfaced by `/tools/configs`. Create a new `SharePointConfig(CodeMieToolConfig)` in a new file `src/codemie_tools/data_management/sharepoint/models.py`:
+++
+++```python
+++class SharePointConfig(CodeMieToolConfig):
+++    credential_type: CredentialTypes = Field(default=CredentialTypes.SHAREPOINT, ...)
+++    url: str = RequiredField(
+++        description="SharePoint tenant root URL",
+++        json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_SHAREPOINT_TOOL_URL")},
+++    )
+++```
+++
+++`SettingsService` mapping for SharePoint does not need to change — existing `url` key already maps through `SHAREPOINT_FIELDS`.
+++
+++---
+++
+++## Out of scope
+++
+++- `ZephyrSquadConfig.DEFAULT_BASE_URL` (`api_wrapper.py`) — vendor SaaS constant, not user-configurable.
+++- `SQLConfig` — uses `host + port` pattern, no URL field.
+++
+++---
+++
+++## Deployment
+++
+++`deploy-templates/values.yaml` must gain one entry per new env var (empty value, filled per deployment):
