++## Prerequisite changes
++
++### ZephyrConfig — add Field metadata without changing required semantics
++
++`src/codemie_tools/qa/zephyr/models.py` currently has `url: str` (bare annotation, no `Field`). Pydantic v2 treats this as required — `ZephyrConfig` without `url` raises `ValidationError`. Using `RequiredField` (which sets `default=""`) would silently weaken that to app-level enforcement. Instead, add `Field(...)` with no `default` to preserve the pydantic-required behaviour while adding the placeholder metadata:
++
++```python
++# Before
++url: str
++
++# After — no semantic change, adds placeholder only
++url: str = Field(
++    description="Zephyr Scale API URL",
++    json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_ZEPHYR_TOOL_URL")},
++)
++```
++
++### SharePointConfig — new model
++
++`SharePointCredentials` (`src/codemie/rest_api/models/settings.py`) is a plain `BaseModel` outside the toolkit hierarchy, so it is not surfaced by `/tools/configs`. Create a new `SharePointConfig(CodeMieToolConfig)` in a new file `src/codemie_tools/data_management/sharepoint/models.py`:
++
++```python
++class SharePointConfig(CodeMieToolConfig):
++    credential_type: CredentialTypes = Field(default=CredentialTypes.SHAREPOINT, ...)
++    url: str = RequiredField(
++        description="SharePoint tenant root URL",
++        json_schema_extra={"placeholder": config_url("DEFAULT_SHAREPOINT_TOOL_URL")},
++    )
++```
++
++`SettingsService` mapping for SharePoint does not need to change — existing `url` key already maps through `SHAREPOINT_FIELDS`.
